## P0 — this repo is public, and staying that way

### [x] Repo visibility — decided: stays public

Rafael's call, 2026-08-15: no need to make `rafiti052/valmorian` private. Recorded here
so it does not get re-litigated every time someone notices `sources/`.

The consequence is that option 3 below is now the operating rule, not a choice:
**`sources/` is curated, not wholesale-committed.** Rafael's own prose can go in; nothing
third-party does.

### [ ] Keep third-party material out of the public repo

Not a preference — this is what makes a public `sources/` safe. Currently untracked and
must stay that way unless the rights are cleared:

- **Commercial rulebook** — `dampd-5e---livro-do-jogador-2024.pdf` (36 MB), the pt-BR
  D&D 2024 Player's Handbook. Publishing it is straightforward copyright infringement.
  Already guarded by `.gitignore`; see the item below.
- **VTT / map art** — `Mapas/` (92 MB) and `Cenarios/` (111 MB). Likely purchased or
  licensed art whose licence does not cover public redistribution. Check the licences
  before any of it is committed.
- **Third-party homebrew** — `updated-my-amphitari-race-...webp`, a Reddit user's
  Amphitari species art. Needs attribution and permission, or it stays out.
- **Player material** — `Ficha *.pdf`, `Backstories.pdf`, and `sources/Yara/`. Other
  people's creative work, and filled sheets carry real names; one filename under
  `sources/Yara/` is a player's real first name, so even the directory listing leaks.
  This one is not yours to decide alone — worth asking the table before it goes public.

Ingestion still works on all of it: the companion reads the working tree, so these files
being untracked costs nothing day to day. What it costs is that `sources[].resource`
provenance links to them resolve only on your machine. That is the trade the public-repo
decision buys, and it is a fine trade.

Practical rule when committing from `sources/`: **add files by name, never `git add
sources/`.**

### [x] Stop the rulebook from being committed by accident

`.gitignore` now excludes `dampd-5e*.pdf` and the `livro-do-jogador` /
`players-handbook` name patterns. The file stays on disk — the companion reads the
working tree, so ingestion still works — it just cannot enter git history.

Note this only helps going forward. It was never committed, so there is nothing to purge
from history yet. That stays true only as long as P0 above is respected.

