### [ ] Clear out the scaffold examples

`codex/` has 10 concept files and some are seeded placeholders rather than real canon —
`codex/party/exemplo-pj.md` most obviously. Decide per file: promote to real canon,
or delete. A placeholder that survives into a populated codex reads as canon six months
from now.

### [ ] Decide on `sources/.gitkeep`

Currently staged as deleted. It was there to keep an empty directory in git; the
directory has 80 files now, so the deletion is correct — this item exists only so the
call is recorded rather than looking like an accident later.

### [ ] Decide how binary assets live in git

Mostly deferred by the public-repo decision: the 288 MB of PNG/JPG in `Mapas/` and
`Cenarios/` is staying untracked for licence reasons anyway. Revisit only if some of that
art turns out to be yours or freely licensed and worth committing — git does not
delta-compress binaries, so every clone would pay for every revision of every map. Git
LFS is the answer if that day comes, and it is much easier to set up before the first big
commit than after. No single file is over GitHub's 100 MB hard limit today.

